Shoals.Curves.yield_curve_tagged: pillar times must be strictly increasing: index 2 has time 2.0, which does not exceed time 3.0 at index 1

The tagged constructor differs from `yield_curve_from_pillars` only in the
`CurveKind` it stores, so it returned the same wrong 0.025 for the same
reordered pillars. It is named in no issue: the defect was reported against two
constructors and there are four exported entry points that take the pillar
times directly. The module has already been through one incomplete enumeration
of its own entry points (shoals#78, whose two-function list missed
`bootstrap_grad_diagonal`), which is why this case is pinned by name.
